    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now suppose you only see the effective speeds:\n\nDownstream = 18 km/hr\nUpstream = 10 km/hr\n\nAdd them: 28. The current cancels, so 28 = 2 × still-water speed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "That gives two useful reverse rules:\n\nStill-water speed = (downstream + upstream) ÷ 2\nCurrent speed = (downstream − upstream) ÷ 2\n\nFor 18 and 10: still water = 14, current = 4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
