    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One effective speed plus the current is also enough.\n\nSuppose downstream speed is 15 km/hr and current is 2.5 km/hr.\n\nStill water = 15 − 2.5 = 12.5\nUpstream = 12.5 − 2.5 = 10 km/hr.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A quick shortcut appears:\n\nUpstream = downstream − 2 × current\nDownstream = upstream + 2 × current\n\nWhy twice? The current changes from +v to −v, a swing of 2v.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
