    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's combine distance, time, and the river model.\n\nSuppose a boat covers 32 km downstream in 6 hours and 14 km upstream in 6 hours.\n\nDownstream = 32/6 = 16/3\nUpstream = 14/6 = 7/3 km/hr.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The current is half their difference:\n\n[(16/3) − (7/3)] ÷ 2\n= (9/3) ÷ 2\n= 3 ÷ 2\n= 1.5 km/hr.\n\nThe fractions look awkward, but the subtraction becomes simple.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
